## Database & Models
- Use Eloquent ORM for database operations instead of raw queries
- Define proper relationships in your models (hasMany, belongsTo, etc.)
- Use model factories and seeders for testing and development
- Implement soft deletes when appropriate instead of permanent deletion
- Use database migrations for all schema changes
- Leverage model observers for complex model events

## Security
- Implement proper authentication and authorization using Laravel's built-in systems
- Use Gates and Policies for permission management
- Always validate all user input with request validation classes
- Implement proper CSRF protection on all forms
- Use prepared statements to prevent SQL injection
- Store sensitive credentials in environment variables, not in code

## Architecture
- Keep controllers thin and use service classes for business logic
- Follow SOLID principles in your code organization
- Use repositories for data access when dealing with complex queries
- Implement proper dependency injection using Laravel's service container
- Use traits to share functionality between classes
- Implement interfaces for key components to make them swappable

## Performance
- Use eager loading to avoid N+1 query problems
- Implement caching strategies for expensive operations
- Use queued jobs for resource-intensive processes
- Configure proper indexes on database tables
- Optimize database queries using query builder or raw queries when necessary
- Use Laravel's route caching in production

## Development
- Use Laravel's event system for decoupling components
- Implement proper error handling and logging
- Use middleware for request/response filtering
- Utilize Laravel's built-in validation system
- Follow PSR standards for code style
- Document your code properly with PHPDoc comments
